Title: check-cross-pr-ticket-collision reports a false collision when run outside CI
Created: 2026-10-12
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-10-12T16:57Z Minh Ha-Duong created
2026-10-13T09:38Z Minh-Ha-Duong note raid Imagine: EXECUTE; self PR inference preserves explicit override and no-ticket fast path; Blind-Spot requires lookup-failure visibility and no false renumber recommendation; exit criteria unchanged.

--- body ---
## Context

`scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh` excludes this PR from its sibling
scan only through the `SELF_PR_NUMBER` environment variable, which only
`.github/workflows/CI.yml` sets. Run interactively from a worktree whose branch
already has an open PR, it reports that PR's own ticket as a rival claim:

    COLLISION: ticket ID 1089 is also added by open PR #1374 (branch t1084-roar-close-and-clean).
    exit 1

Observed on 2026-10-12 while checking the `t1084-roar-close-and-clean` branch
before a merge decision. CI is unaffected — it passes
`github.event.pull_request.number`. The exposure is an agent that runs the gate
locally, believes the report and renumbers a ticket that never collided, which
breaks the ticket ID and every cross-reference to it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] With `SELF_PR_NUMBER` unset, the script resolves its own PR from the current branch (forge call marked `harness-extension-point`) and excludes it; when the branch has no open PR it scans the full sibling list
- [ ] Run from a worktree whose branch has an open PR adding a ticket file, it exits 0 with that PR excluded, verified against a real open PR
- [ ] Positive control: a genuine sibling collision is still reported when two open PRs add the same ID and the script runs from one of them
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Raid plan — 2026-10-13

Actions: preserve explicit SELF_PR_NUMBER and the no-ticket fast path; infer this PR with a marked forge lookup when unset. A lookup failure is not proof of no PR: use the successfully fetched open-PR list/current branch to disambiguate, report uncertainty and never recommend renumbering on an uncertain self claim. Update forge-coupling documentation.

First test: unset SELF_PR_NUMBER; own PR claims the added ID, a sibling claims a distinct ID; expect exit 0 and no own-PR file fetch. Positive control: sibling claims same ID and is named with exit 1. Cover lookup miss/failure, no open PR, override and unreadable forge. Validate against a real open PR as required.

Files: scripts/check-cross-pr-ticket-collision.sh; tests/test_check_cross_pr_ticket_collision.sh; this ticket. Dependencies: git, gh, jq and existing hermetic shell fixtures. No new library. Exit criteria unchanged.
